# apps/mock-engine/.dockerignore — W9-I
# mock-engine builds with THIS directory as the context
# (`docker build apps/mock-engine`), so this file is fully effective.
# Keep src/ IN the context (that is all the trivial runner needs); keep
# everything else out — especially the zero-dep guarantee: no node_modules,
# no lockfiles, no .env secrets in a test-helper image.
#
# W9-I ignore set: node_modules, .next, dist, tests, .demo-output, .env*,
# fixtures (+ .git/coverage hygiene). **/ forms cover nested copies.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
tests
**/tests
.demo-output
**/.demo-output
.env*
**/.env*
fixtures
**/fixtures
.git
**/.git
coverage
**/coverage
